# S3 fixture ("created as Excel shows it"): a table with a total row, conditional formats and data
# validation, through s3-data's Insert > Table, Conditional formatting and Data Validation (their
# script ops on the selection), values typed in the en-NL region. Excel shows a total row's formula
# without the table's name ([OK]), and a list's items with the region's separator (Yes;No).
sheet-name "Sales"
enter A1 "Region"
enter B1 "Q1"
enter C1 "Q2"
enter D1 "OK"
enter A2 "North"
enter B2 "120"
enter C2 "340"
enter A3 "South"
enter B3 "80"
enter C3 "95"
enter A4 "East"
enter B4 "260"
enter C4 "410"
enter A5 "West"
enter B5 "150"
enter C5 "60"
table A1:D5 TableStyleMedium9
table-total A1
rule B2:C5 greater "200"
rule C2:C5 bar
rule A2:A5 formula "=$C2<100"
validation D2:D5 list "Yes|No"
validation B2:B5 whole between "0" "1000"
enter D2 "Yes"
enter D4 "No"
save
expect table Table1 Sales!A1:D6 style TableStyleMedium9 totals True
expect cell Sales!A6 text Total
expect cell Sales!D6 formula =SUBTOTAL(103,[OK])
expect cell Sales!D6 text 2
expect rule Sales!B2:C5 type 1 operator 5
expect rule Sales!C2:C5 type 4 operator
expect rule Sales!A2:A5 type 2 operator
expect validation Sales!D2:D5 type 3 Yes;No
expect validation Sales!B2:B5 type 1 0
